# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js (App Router) project following the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **File**: `package.json`
- **Action**: Added `@vercel/analytics` (v2.0.1) to dependencies
- **Method**: Ran `npm install @vercel/analytics`

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **File**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the MantineProvider closing tag
  
### 3. Lock File Update
- **File**: `package-lock.json`
- **Action**: Updated to include @vercel/analytics and its dependencies (244 new packages)

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart guide for Next.js App Router:
- Imported the Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/next` (framework-specific import)
- Placed the component in the root layout.tsx file within the body tag
- Positioned after other providers and integrations to maintain existing functionality

## Framework Context
- **Framework**: Next.js 15.2.6 (App Router)
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Analytics Package Version**: @vercel/analytics@2.0.1

## Verification Steps Completed
✅ Package successfully installed
✅ Dependencies updated (244 packages added)
✅ Build completed successfully (42 routes generated without errors)
✅ Code structure preserved (existing components and integrations remain intact)
✅ TypeScript compilation successful

## Next Steps (Post-Deployment)
After deploying to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Navigate to the Analytics tab and click "Enable"
3. Verify analytics collection by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`
4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after user visits

## Notes
- The Analytics component is placed after the MantineProvider but still inside the body tag, following the documentation's recommendation
- The component is lightweight and won't impact page performance
- Analytics data will only be collected when deployed to Vercel and after enabling it in the dashboard
- The build completed successfully with no errors or warnings related to the analytics integration
